Design choices:
- Add HTML joystick markup, remove move buttons.
- Keep jump/throw as circular-ish buttons stacked vertically to the right of joystick? Current pad is bottom anchored. Layout: flex row; joystick then actions column. For p2 mirrored? P2 is on right side of screen; joystick should probably be left of actions too? For right-handed thumb on right side, actions should be at far right and joystick to the left of them? Hmm, for two-player on one phone, P1 left half: joystick far left, buttons to its right. P2 right half: mirrored: buttons far right, joystick to its left (toward center). Actually typical: each player's joystick on the outer edge and action buttons toward center? For P1 joystick left, action right; for P2 joystick right, action left (mirrored). That avoids both joysticks near center. P2 pad anchored right, flex-direction row-reverse so joystick on right, buttons left. Yes.

But then pads may overlap in portrait (each pad width ~ joystick 104 + gap 8 + buttons 58 = 170; screen 390 => 340 fits barely with margins 9 each = 358; okay). Pause mini center bottom may overlap? Pads occupy full bottom; pause mini is center; pad p1 left width 170, p2 right width 170 -> center gap 32 for pause (36 wide) slight overlap. Could put pause mini above center bottom (bottom + 70). Better: position pause-mini bottom around 8px but joystick occupies bottom; center gap maybe. In portrait 390 width: p1 from 9 to 179, p2 from 211 to 381, center 179-211 = 32, pause 36 -> slight overlap. Could shrink joystick to 92 on narrow and buttons 52. Or place pause mini at top center? There is HUD. Simpler: `bottom: calc(max(8px, env(...)) + 4px)` and shrink via media query (max-width 460): joystick 88px, buttons 50px, gap 6 => total 144*2+18=306, plenty. Use clamp for joystick: clamp(84px, 12vh, 118px). At 844 height 12vh = 101. Buttons clamp(48px, 7vh, 62px). Width = 84+6+48=138 each at min; fine.

Landscape short height 560: 12vh=67 -> clamp min 84. Apron = clamp(H*.27,96,134) => 151? H 390 landscape => apron 105. Joystick 84 + bottom 7 fits 91 < 105. Jump/throw 48*2 + gap = 102 fits barely. Good. But arena floor y = H - apron; touch controls overlay under floor (apron). Fine.

Need joystick base visual: 100% size, translucent cream with colored ring per player, inner ring, knob centered. Add arrows hint (◀ ▶) subtly? Could add left/right chevrons inside base or a crosshair. Since it's a horizontal-only joystick in a platformer, knob can move in all directions visually but only x used. Maybe constrain knob movement to horizontal track? That would look like a slider! No — allow full circular movement, use x. Add label "MOVE" small under? Keep simple.

Actually: if vertical movement is unused, users dragging up may expect jump. Could map up-flick to jump (queueJump when joystick crosses up threshold) — nice bonus. And down could... nothing. We can implement up gesture to jump: on pointermove, if dy < -0.55*max and !jumpLatch => queueJump(p), jumpLatch=true; reset when dy > -0.35*max. This adds intuitive vertical input. But jump button exists. Might cause accidental jumps. I'll include it with a clear label? Hmm. Keep it: joystick up = jump, documented? Could be nice, but risk. The task just says joystick. I'll implement horizontal movement only and full visual movement. Document "drag to move".

Accessibility: joystick as div with role="application" and aria-label. Keyboard already available.

Pointer handling details:
- pointerdown on joystick: use base rect center. If pads are positioned, base rect fine. But pointerdown could start anywhere within the "joystick" 100% box. Set knob to pointer offset immediately.
- pointerId ownership per joystick. Use `joy.pointerId` and setPointerCapture on the joystick element.
- On pointerup/cancel/lostpointercapture: reset.
- Handle multi-touch: each joystick independent; pointer capture per element.
- prevent browser gestures: touch-action:none; also preventDefault on pointerdown/move.

State: `touchAxes = [0,0]`. When releasing, set 0 immediately (no inertia) — player physics decelerates.

Deadzone: 0.16, rescale: `const a = (mag - dz)/(1-dz)` times sign. Actually dx/max after clamp gives -1..1. axis = sign*clamp((abs-dz)/(1-dz),0,1).

Knob clamp to radius = base*0.30 maybe; knob size 46% so knob stays inside. maxOffset = baseRect.width*0.30 (radius of base 0.5 minus knob radius 0.23 = 0.27). Use 0.28.

