content.text:
Now JS changes in game-play.js.

1. Replace `const touchDirs = [new Set(), new Set()];` with axes plus pointer map.
2. getInputDir use axes.
3. bindTouch rewrite, add bindJoysticks.
4. pauseGame clearing.
5. blur clearing.
6. Call bindJoysticks in boot (game-ui.js).
7. Reset joysticks on newMatch/startRound maybe startRound.

Let me implement carefully.

Current input section:
```js
const keys = new Set();
const touchDirs = [new Set(), new Set()];
const pointerOwners = new Map();
```

New:
```js
const keys = new Set();
const touchAxes = [0, 0];          // analog joystick output, -1..1
const joysticks = [];
let joyPointers = new Map(); // maybe not needed
```
pointerOwners is only used by touch buttons for ownership; we can keep for buttons (jump/throw) and separate joy pointerId on each joystick object.

getInputDir:
```js
  const axis = touchAxes[p.idx];
  if (axis) dir += axis;
  return clamp(dir, -1, 1);
```
Also `p.facing = dir` fix to Math.sign.

bindTouch: only buttons. Keep `pointerOwners` map. Remove left/right handling.

bindJoysticks:
```js
function bindJoysticks() {
  joysticks.length = 0;
  document.querySelectorAll('#touch .joystick').forEach(joyEl => {
    const pad = joyEl.closest('.pad');
    const pIdx = Number(pad.dataset.player);
    const base = joyEl.querySelector('.stick-base');
    const knob = joyEl.querySelector('.stick-knob');
    const state = { el: joyEl, base, knob, pIdx, pointerId: null, max: 0 };
    joysticks.push(state);

    const setAxis = (dx, dy, max) => {
      const distRaw = Math.hypot(dx, dy);
      const scale = distRaw > max ? max / distRaw : 1;
      const kx = dx * scale, ky = dy * scale;
      state.knob.style.transform = `translate(-50%, -50%) translate(${kx}px, ${ky}px)`;
      const dead = 0.16;
      const raw = clamp(kx / max, -1, 1);
      const mag = Math.abs(raw);
      touchAxes[pIdx] = Math.sign(raw) * clamp((mag - dead) / (1 - dead), 0, 1);
    };
    const release = e => {
      if (state.pointerId === null) return;
      if (e && e.pointerId !== state.pointerId) return;
      state.pointerId = null;
      touchAxes[pIdx] = 0;
      joyEl.classList.remove('active');
      knob.style.transform = 'translate(-50%, -50%)';
    };
    const place = e => {
      const r = base.getBoundingClientRect();
      state.max = r.width * 0.3;
      if (!state.max) return { dx: 0, dy: 0 };
      return { dx: e.clientX - (r.left + r.width / 2), dy: e.clientY - (r.top + r.height / 2) };
    };
    joyEl.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => {
      e.preventDefault();
      ensureAudio();
      if (state.pointerId !== null) return;
      if ((state !== 'play' && state !== 'title') || paused) return;
      state.pointerId = e.pointerId;
      joyEl.classList.add('active');
      try { joyEl.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); } catch {}
      const { dx, dy } = place(e);
      setAxis(dx, dy, state.max || 1);
    });
    joyEl.addEventListener('pointermove', e => {
      if (state.pointerId !== e.pointerId) return;
      e.preventDefault();
      const { dx, dy } = place(e);
      setAxis(dx, dy, state.max || 1);
    });
    ['pointerup', 'pointercancel', 'lostpointercapture'].forEach(type =>
      joyEl.addEventListener(type, release));
    joyEl.addEventListener('contextmenu', e => e.preventDefault());
  });
}
```
Issue: state name collides with global `state` variable! Inside object state and global state. Use `joy` object named `j`. In `pointerdown` check global state. Good.

`j.max` set in place before setAxis, and in pointerdown we compute max before setAxis. place sets max.

On pointerdown, if touch starts at edge, knob jumps and axis immediately. Fine.

`lostpointercapture` fires after pointerup release; pointerId already null, fine.

Reset:
```js
function resetJoysticks() {
  touchAxes[0] = touchAxes[1] = 0;
  for (const j of joysticks) {
    j.pointerId = null;
    j.el.classList.remove('active');
    j.knob.style.transform = 'translate(-50%, -50%)';
  }
  pointerOwners.clear();
  document.querySelectorAll('.tbtn.pressed').forEach(b => b.classList.remove('pressed'));
}
```

pauseGame uses resetJoysticks instead of touchDirs.

Blur uses resetJoysticks.

Also in newMatch/startRound? When a round ends charging etc, joystick may remain held. That's fine. But when startRound resets positions, if user still holds joystick, they'll move. Could reset on finishRound/startRound to be safe. Add resetJoysticks() in startRound? It clears axes; user must release/repress (pointer still captured but axis 0; pointermove re-sets though). Fine.

Also when pause overlay appears and player holds joystick, reset.

bindTouch still needs pointerOwners for buttons. Keep.

Also note `state` global check in joystick handlers.

Touch jump/throw buttons handling: `pointerOwners` only used there. Fine.

