Now modify bindJoysticks to add jump on up and fire logic. We need to know if player is moving. We can check `Math.abs(touchAxes[pIdx]) > 0.2` or keyboard. Simpler: `isMoving = Math.abs(touchAxes[pIdx]) > 0.15`. But at pointerdown, touchAxes is 0 initially. We can determine movement by keyboard keys for that player or joystick x after setAxis. We'll set axis first, then decide.

Let's update bindJoysticks:
- Add `jumpLatch: false` to joystick state.
- In setAxis, after computing x, y, add jump handling:
```js
const upThreshold = 0.55;
if (dy < -upThreshold * j.max && !j.jumpLatch) {
  j.jumpLatch = true;
  const p = players[pIdx];
  if (p) queueJump(p);
}
if (dy > -0.25 * j.max) j.jumpLatch = false;
```
