But if the user holds the button while standing still, we don't want to auto-release and then re-press? The pointerdown fires once. We'll auto-release after 90ms, producing a quick shot. If they keep holding, no further action until pointerup (which calls releaseThrowInput again, harmless). Good.

For moving case, don't auto-release; release on pointerup.

