Could be a request to redo the drop-through? Or redo the entire game? Unclear. I should ask? The instruction says don't ask clarifying questions. Make reasonable assumption: "Redo" means redo the previous feature (drop-through) maybe improve it. But what to change?

Alternatively, "Redo" could be a command to redo the last edit (like Ctrl+Z redo) in the game? Not applicable.

Maybe the user wants me to redo the whole task from scratch? That would be wasteful.

Given the pattern of short requests, "Redo" might mean "redo the last change" because it didn't work. The last change: joystick down makes fall from platforms. Maybe it didn't work on their device. We could improve: ensure drop-through works even if not moving, and make it more reliable. Or maybe they want to redo the control scheme entirely.

Let's improve drop-through: currently dropThrough timer 0.25s. If the player is on a platform and pushes down, they should drop. But the platform collision skip only helps if vy becomes positive. When standing on a platform, vy=0. Pushing down doesn't add downward velocity. Need to give a small downward push when dropping. Let's modify: when dropThrough set, also set p.vy = Math.max(p.vy, 120*S) and p.onGround=false. That initiates fall. Let's add in the down-input handling in updatePlayer and bindJoysticks.

